Hi Mike,
Thanks for your reply and sharing, the project sounds interesting! I'm looking forward to the finishing.

I still some questions, my apologies if I misunderstand.

Firstly, according to your discussion with  Matt, wether the QMET equal to 0.0056*O2_ml - Oxygen consumption rate (ml/h) ? but in the results of my code is not equal to 0.0056.

Secondly, I found in some coordinates, It's not always a linear relationship between O2_ml - Oxygen consumption rate (ml/h) and QMET, it's affected by rainact? when I changed the rainact from 1 to 0, It's always a linear relationship, but the coordinate in (110,35) remain the same question.

Best wishes,

Zhong-wen

below is my code.

library(NicheMapR)

micro<-micro_global(loc = c(98.91667,36.91667),run.gads = 2,timeinterval = 365,soiltype = 1)
lizard_loc<-ectotherm( live=1, nyears = 1,rainact = 1, actrainthresh = 0.1)

lizard_enbal_out<- data.frame(lizard_loc[["enbal"]])
lizard_masbal_out<- data.frame(lizard_loc[["masbal"]])

plot(lizard_masbal_out$O2_ml,lizard_enbal_out$QMET)

